{"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "SessionStart", "additionalContext": "Harness global AGENTS.md, part 3/4:
**Work in progress:** Home explicitly names the active lanes and sizes that set to the budget, with no fixed lane cap. Use fewer lanes for larger models, higher reasoning, fast mode or a distant weekly reset; use more for smaller models, lower reasoning, standard speed or allowance that would expire near reset. Act only on lanes Home names, including any it names to drain. Resume and account pooling may continue only those lanes and their children; never revive unnamed or backlogged lanes. Only Home opens top-level threads: backlog lanes from groomed, specced items, replacements for named lanes, and its own scratch runners such as lage. New work defaults to a backlog issue. Child work stays under its assigned lane. Process's existing verification rollout may run at most three existing coverage-table Verify workers at once; park the rest with a backlog note, settle each merged or parked worker, and resume the next only when a slot is free. Open no Verify threads beyond that coverage table. Policy: phaedrus, 2026-10-21.

**Review links:** Every agent report, question and `home post` entry must give clickable, accessible links to everything phaedrus needs to review. Use GitHub or live URLs; preserve native clickable T3 thread links (`[title](t3-thread://v1/<threadId>)`). For local previews, screenshots, briefs and other evidence, copy only the reviewed evidence into a dedicated, secret-free directory under `~/.local/share/harness/review-evidence/<lane>-<topic>/`, then publish it with `sudo -n tailscale serve --bg --set-path /<lane>-<topic>/ <target>` on the host yourself. If the host lacks passwordless Serve permission, use an available GitHub or live URL instead of publishing a filesystem tree. Provide `https://<host>.tail5f5eb4.ts.net/...`; verify reachability before posting and keep it served until the item is decided, then remove only your handler (`sudo -n tailscale serve --set-path /<lane>-<topic>/ off`). Never take `/` or an occupied path, reset Serve, or remove a handler you did not create. He cannot open local paths or run server commands: never substitute a bare path, localhost/file URL or command for accessible evidence. Keep tailnet evidence private; never use a public tunnel or Funnel.

**Act without asking:**
- read-only work anywhere, including read-only production queries;
- pushing your own branches, opening PRs and re-running CI;
- publishing tickets that follow from scope he confirmed;
- fixing bugs you find: code through a PR; shared hosts too, unless that destroys or widens anything;
- deploying merged code through the repository's own pipeline;
- restoring a release that hurts users (`release-watch`).

**Merge** your own PR in every organization on a judge's SHIP after independent QA and review plus passing checks, using [ship-loop's rigor tiers](skill://ship-loop/roles.md#rigor). Documents, briefs and measurements use the light tier: one combined QA and review agent on a cheap model, then an independent judge, unless a higher-tier trigger applies. Only machine-generated, generator-only release PRs merge on passing checks alone (`docs/principles/007-braver-engineers-continuous-deployment.md`). Never request human review.

**Bring him only** (Foundations' ask-first list, plus product intent):
- product intent the spec doesn't settle;
- destructive or irreversible acts, such as deleting data, repositories, machines or accounts, force-pushing a shared branch, or a migration a revert can't undo;
- writes to production data;
- spending money;
- creating, widening or revoking credentials;
- effects on third parties, such as messages to people outside the team.

Verification's explicitly scoped AgentMail QA setup is the narrow exception to the credentials and production-data ask-first rules above. Shared HOUSEHOLD_MEMBERS changes remain Process-only under Verification's complete-baseline procedure. All other credential and production-data changes still require permission.

